From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:25:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xl2tpd: do not start at boot

/lib/netifd/proto/l2tp.sh starts xl2tpd on demand with
/etc/init.d/xl2tpd restart when its control pipe or process is missing,
so starting it at boot only spends RAM on routers without an L2TP WAN.
A UCI change of xl2tp still triggers a reload once the service is
running; a router running xl2tpd as an LNS server can start it from
/etc/rc.local.
---
 net/xl2tpd/files/xl2tpd.init | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/xl2tpd/files/xl2tpd.init b/net/xl2tpd/files/xl2tpd.init
index a6d7f1c..5e44092 100644
--- a/net/xl2tpd/files/xl2tpd.init
+++ b/net/xl2tpd/files/xl2tpd.init
@@ -94,6 +94,13 @@ service_triggers() {
 	procd_add_reload_trigger xl2tp
 }
 
+boot() {
+	# /lib/netifd/proto/l2tp.sh starts xl2tpd on demand when an L2TP
+	# interface comes up, so do not keep it in RAM on routers without L2TP.
+	# An LNS server can add /etc/init.d/xl2tpd start to /etc/rc.local.
+	return 0
+}
+
 start_service() {
 	rm -rf "$RUN_D"
 	mkdir -p "$RUN_D"
